# Start PostgreSQL:  docker compose -f deploy/docker-compose.yml up -d
# Create a key:      dotnet run --project tools/Relay.Cli -- keys create --tenant demo
# Run the API:       dotnet run --project src/Relay.Api
# Paste the printed key below. Never commit a real key.

@host = http://localhost:5238
@apiKey = paste-your-key-here

### Health (no key needed)
GET {{host}}/health

### Send a message (idempotent: repeat with the same key and body to get the same id)
# @name send
POST {{host}}/v1/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Idempotency-Key: demo-1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "to": ["recipient@example.test"],
  "subject": "Hello from Relay",
  "html": "<p>It works.</p>",
  "text": "It works."
}

### Get that message with its timeline
GET {{host}}/v1/messages/{{send.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}

### List messages, newest first
GET {{host}}/v1/messages?limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}

### Missing key -> 401 ProblemDetails
GET {{host}}/v1/messages

### Header injection -> 400 ValidationProblem
POST {{host}}/v1/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "to": ["recipient@example.test"],
  "subject": "Hi\r\nBcc: victim@example.test",
  "text": "x"
}

### OpenAPI document (browse {{host}}/docs for the Scalar reference)
GET {{host}}/openapi/v1.json
